      "content": "Optimize a BF16 SwiGLU GPU kernel on RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell SM120, 188 SM, 128 MiB L2.\nEach turn submit exactly one JSON tool call, no markdown:\n{\"tool\":\"evaluate\",\"code\":\"complete Python module defining run(x)\",\"reason\":\"brief hypothesis\"}\nYou must CHANGE the starting kernel and make a different concrete optimization each turn. Do not resubmit identical source. Explain which operation or launch geometry you changed. Duplicate Python ASTs are rejected without benchmarking. You must author the full candidate kernel code. Imports: import torch, import triton, import triton.language as tl.\nOnly imports and functions at top level. No file, network, process access, introspection, reference or validator access.\nInput contiguous BF16 [T,24576]. Return fresh BF16 [T,12288] equal to silu(first half)*second half. No input mutation.\nTraining T=1 and T=7239, actual layer-0 Qwen3-8B inputs. Fixed vLLM native reference, atol=rtol=0.0078125, no failing elements.\nMinimize sum of CUDA Graph median microseconds over both shapes. Five warmups, 11 trials, 10 calls per graph.\nYou receive correctness and timing after each submission. You cannot change this evaluator, tolerance or score.\nThere are at most six candidates within 60 seconds charged inference wall time plus evaluation event windows.\nThe original model trace has 36 prefill SwiGLU calls totaling 11204.399 us and 36 decode calls totaling 78.080 us.\nInitial measured native graph times: 2.7008 us (T=1), 351.824 us (T=7239). Compiler expression: 0.8928, 348.832 us.\nThis run uses an exclusive GPU. The starting kernel launches BLOCK=256 and num_warps=4; submitting those unchanged is a duplicate. Make a concrete change, such as a different block size or shape specialization. Every passing candidate receives actual CUDA profiler kernel names, durations and launch dimensions in tool feedback. Use those observations for your next hypothesis. Profiler durations are instrumented and are not the timing score.\nAllowed attribute names: abs, arange, bfloat16, cdiv, constexpr, contiguous, device, dtype, empty, empty_like, exp, exp2, float, float16, float32, full, functional, int32, jit, load, log, max, max_contiguous, maximum, minimum, multiple_of, next_power_of_2, nn, numel, program_id, reshape, rsqrt, shape, sigmoid, silu, sqrt, store, stride, sum, tanh, to, view, where, zeros\nActual exclusive-device profiler observations for the starting BLOCK256/4warps kernel: [{\"t\": 1, \"profiler_feedback\": {\"trace\": \"3-schedule-profile-1.json\", \"kernels\": [{\"name\": \"Kernel\", \"duration_us\": 0.832, \"grid\": [48, 1, 1], \"block\": [128, 1, 1], \"stream\": 7}], \"scope\": \"instrumented CUDA kernel activity; not hardware counters or timing score\"}, \"median_graph_us\": 1.0495999827980995}, {\"t\": 7239, \"profiler_feedback\": {\"trace\": \"3-schedule-profile-7239.json\", \"kernels\": [{\"name\": \"Kernel\", \"duration_us\": 341.915, \"grid\": [347472, 1, 1], \"block\": [128, 1, 1], \"stream\": 7}], \"scope\": \"instrumented CUDA kernel activity; not hardware counters or timing score\"}, \"median_graph_us\": 348.1247901916504}]"
